Notes
This page REPLACES the COHERENT 4.2 Lexicon article of the same name.  Nothing
of Mark Williams Company's text remains in what you are reading.  The article
describes a ps that reads /dev/ps, prints the controlling terminal as `tty44:',
lists symbolic sleep events, and takes -e and -p; this one reads the process
table through /dev/kmem, has a three-column TTY field, prints event addresses,
and has no -e and no -p.  The fields themselves are the article's, and are
named here as it names them.

Each process can overwrite its own command name and arguments, so the command
column is what the process says it is.  The system also keeps running while ps
walks the table: two lines of one listing need not describe the same instant.
